  "notes": "Original mechanism schematic. Panel a shows schematic observations and ordered cumulative-sales quantiles, not measured values. Panel b uses matched illustrative residual marks, not empirical values or counts. R2 uses eligible mature residuals across versions; R3 keeps only the current version. Groups, window and output sorting remain identical. Panel c requires s+H+d≤t before issue. Panel d is the analytic binary availability example: H14/U28/d0, initially empty pool, complete labels, W≥H, one finite same-group residual sufficient. R2 [14,84); R3 [14,28),[42,56),[70,84). Availability does not mean nonzero correction. Scientific source: current manuscript Methods 3.4–3.5 and figure_source_data/figure1_design.json. Visual references inspected: Bodnar et al., Nature 2025, Fig.1 (https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-025-09005-y); Lee et al., ICML 2025, Fig.1 (https://proceedings.mlr.press/v267/lee25ag.html); Im and Kwon, ICLR 2026, Fig.1 (https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2026/hash/2a8ce71baac4c89bf9ff479d8240c7d9-Abstract-Conference.html). References inform functional glyphs, hierarchy and explicit temporal pathways only. No figure elements or paper artwork are reproduced."
